title: Dashboard › Requests table › Sort the rows
route: /dashboard
intro: Five headings of the Requests table sort the rows. Each is a button, so the keyboard works too. A heading goes ascending, then descending, then back to the app's own order. The sort is not saved in the address.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Dashboard is open\nHeadings of the 'Requests' table"
screen h1 "Five headings can sort\nCase, Payer, Where it is, Clock, At stake\nEach shows a small up and down arrow"
click c1 "Click a heading\nOr Tab to it and press Enter or Space"
decision d1 "Is this heading already the sorted one?"
process p1 "No: the sort starts on this heading, ascending\nThe arrow points up; the heading is marked ascending for a screen reader"
decision d2 "Which way is it sorted now?"
process p2 "Ascending, so the next click sorts descending\nThe arrow points down"
process p3 "Descending, so the next click clears the sort\nBack to the app's own order\nNeeds you first, then very late, late, denials with under 2 days left, the rest"
process p4 "Rows that tie keep the app's own order"
process p5 "Table goes back to its first 8 rows"
screen sc "Rows in the new order\n'Showing 8 of 39'"

group gKeys "What each heading sorts by"
  screen k1 "Case\nThe ID, A to Z with numbers in order: D-3272 before D-3279, R-0870 before R-1021"
  screen k2 "Payer\nThe short name shown in the row, A to Z: Beacon PPO, Cardinal, Evergreen, Harborview MA, Lakeshore, Summit Medicaid"
  screen k3 "Where it is\nThe stage: Preparing, Received, Under review, Info requested, Approved, then Appeal or call"
  screen k4 "Clock\nThe number in the cell: time left for a denial with a deadline, otherwise time in stage\nRows with a fixed note such as 'decision 11/02' stay last either way"
  screen k5 "At stake\nThe money asked for, smallest first when ascending"
endgroup

process p6 "Filters, the stage tiles and 'Clear filters' keep the sort\nLeaving the page or reloading clears it"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table › Order, rows and paging"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table › Read a row: bars, clock and what happens next"

s1 --> h1 --> c1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p1 --> p4
d1 -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Ascending| p2 --> p4
d2 -->|Descending| p3 --> p5
p4 --> p5 --> sc
sc --> p6 --> g1
h1 --> k1 & k2 & k3 & k4 & k5
k4 -.-> g2
